From 2dff82b601e8db0f9f915b241a3e3b05962435cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Benny Cheung <benny@example.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 22:02:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Fix: player sinking in adventure maps (Ancient Ruins)

Root cause: clampToGround() was calling getGroundHeightAt() which uses
raycast to find terrain. In adventure maps, raycast misses the farm
terrain mesh and falls back to groundY=0, causing player to sink.

Fix: For adventure map detection (|x|>55 or |z|>55), directly use
adventureGroundY instead of calling getGroundHeightAt() to avoid
incorrect raycast fallback to 0.
